# ui/bun.lock is deliberately NOT ignored, for the same reason as go.sum below:
# CI runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in ui/, which has nothing to freeze
# against without it, and the Dockerfile's `COPY ui/bun.lock*` tolerates the
# file being absent. Untracked, UI dependency versions float between builds and
# two builds of the same tag can differ.
# go.sum is deliberately NOT ignored. It is a build input, not build output:
# without it `go build` fails on a clean checkout with "missing go.sum entry"
# for every dependency, which is exactly what happened to CI. It is also the
# only thing verifying that a given module version still contains what it
# contained when it was vendored, so ignoring it removes a supply-chain control
# as well as reproducibility.
/graphify-out/
/.agents
/.claude
/.junie
skills-lock.json
ui/test-results/
/hermod_bin
/ui/hermod_e2e.db
/hermod_e2e.db
/hermod_e2e.db-shm
/hermod_e2e.db-wal
/registry.test
.dev/
layout-audit.json
form-audit.json
# Screenshots and geometry dumps from the sidebar/visual audit — regenerated on
# every run, useful locally and as CI artifacts, never worth committing.
ui/audit-shots/
/audit-shots/

# Ad-hoc artifacts that accumulate in the working tree during local runs and
# debugging. None of them are inputs to a build or a test.
/server.log
/ui.log
/test_results.txt
/test-results/
/dummy.txt
/after_alert.png
/before_alert.png
/hermod_log_e2e.db
/hermod_log_e2e.db-shm
/hermod_log_e2e.db-wal
# SQLite files created when a DSN query string is mistakenly used as a filename.
/?_pragma=*

# --- Build artefacts and test databases -------------------------------------
# These were previously committed (hermodctl at 11 MB, plus SQLite files left
# behind by the registry tests). Patterns rather than paths, so a test that
# writes its scratch database somewhere new does not add it to the next commit.
/hermodctl
/hermod_bin
/registry.test
*.test
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
